610                                                       |
Re-run one of the alignment cycles (500 or 501) and the 
calibration cycle (502) from where this input may be set to
a valid value.
611                                                       |
When programming the cutter profile checking cycle (508),
check that Q374 is correctly entered as either +1 (external)
, -1 (internal), or 0 (both).
612                                                       |
Re-run the measuring cycle that resulted in this error, 
setting Q365/ROFFS to a value smaller than that specified as
the maximum tool radius within the Renishaw set-up table.
Alternatively, increase the value of the maximum tool
radius.
613                                                       |
Re-run one of the alignment cycles (500 or 501) and the
calibration cycle (502) from where this input may be set to 
a valid value.
614                                                       |

615                                                       |
Review the sample size and scatter tolerance requirements.
Check the reason for poor measurement performance and/or
check the sample size and scatter tolerance values entered
in the Renishaw set-up table, defined as number of retries
and scatter tolerance respectively. Poor measurement 
performance can be caused by excessive coolant or swarf on
or around the tool.
616                                                       |
Check the electrical installation.
617                                                       |
Check the maximum tool length specified in the Renishaw
set-up table and the length of the active tool in the tool
table. It may be necessary to alter these, within the limits
of the machine tool.
618                                                       |
Check the minimum tool length specified in the Renishaw
set-up table and the length of the active tool in the tool
table. It may be necessary to alter these, within the limits
of the machine tool.
619                                                       |
Check the minimum tool length specified in the Renishaw
set-up table and the length of the active tool in the tool
table. It may be necessary to alter these, within the limits
of the machine tool.
620                                                       |
If a sister tool is specified for the broken tool, within
the tool table, the broken tool is replaced automatically
when next called. If no sister tool is specified, replace
the tool and establish its new correct dimensions with one
of the length or radius measuring cycles (cycles 503, 504,
505, or 512).
621                                                       |
If the tool is missing or its approximate length
(where required) in the tool table is incorrectly short,
correct this and retry the cycle.
If the NC system has been moved, re-run the alignment and
calibration cycles (500 or 501, and 502) to reset the 
positional values. If the NC system has been moved as the
result of a collision, check it is operating correctly
before running any cycles (see "NC1 installation guide and
parts list", Part No. H-2000-5048).
622                                                       |
If a sister tool is specified for the broken tool, within
the tool table, the broken tool is replaced automatically
when next called. If no sister tool is specified, replace
the tool and establish its new correct basic dimensions with
one of the length or radius measuring cycles (cycles 503,
504, 505, or 512). If the tool does not appear to be broken,
check the tool and holder for eccentric / runout.
623                                                       |
Check that nothing is interfering with the beam and retry
the cycle. If the beam is not cut but the alarm persists,
check the electrical installation.
624                                                       |
M code out of range
625                                                       |
Where the wiring has not been provided for extended cycles,
do not attempt to use these cycles. If wiring connections
and Input / M-code assignment has been carried out, check
the Cycles supported parameter in the Renishaw set-up table.
626                                                       |
Spindle speed > maximum
627                                                       |
Re-run the measuring cycle that resulted in this error,
setting Q365 to a value smaller than that of the active tool
radius (R) in the tool table.
628                                                       |
Re-run the measuring cycle that resulted in this error,
after correcting the Q371 value. If the maximum value
defined in the tool table is in question, contact your
equipment provider for advice.
629                                                       |
If a sister tool is specified for the tool, within the tool 
table, the tool is replaced automatically when next called.
If no sister tool is specified, replace the tool and
establish its new correct dimensions with one of the length
or radius measuring cycles (cycles 503, 504 or 505 ) and
using parameter Q380 (0).
630                                                       |
No further action is required because all the system tests
are good. Prior to this message however, corrective actions
may have been necessary to progress this far.
